{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GhAgGDZFprbER8eWhycHrr","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL Rolling Review review form 2025 2026 overall assessment score scale 1-5\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review Data Collection (ARR-DC) - ARR Data Collection\",\"url\":\"https://arr-data.aclweb.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Dashboard\",\"url\":\"https://stats.aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing\"},{\"title\":\"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \\\"Publish or Perish\\\" Circus | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus\"},{\"title\":\"ACL ARR 2025 May | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FMay\"},{\"title\":\"Incentives 2026 – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about the ACL Rolling Review scoring system for 2025-2026:\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\nHowever, the search results don't provide the specific 1-5 scale details for the overall assessment score in the review form itself. The results indicate that reviewers use these three scoring dimensions, but the exact numerical scale definitions for the overall recommendation score are not fully detailed in the retrieved content.\n\nIf you need more specific information about the exact scale definitions (what 1-5 means for each score), you may want to visit the official ARR review form directly at aclrollingreview.org/reviewform or check the full reviewer guidelines on aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ef33cb85-ae55-46f6-8462-dd61be87818f","uuid":"b5af39c1-1778-4bcd-bb59-b5561674ba40","timestamp":"2026-05-15T14:17:10.762Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review review form 2025 2026 overall assessment score scale 1-5","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01QozmK14ZT6RQWw2neD8Ho1","content":[{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review Data Collection (ARR-DC) - ARR Data Collection","url":"https://arr-data.aclweb.org/"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"ARR Dashboard","url":"https://stats.aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing"},{"title":"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \"Publish or Perish\" Circus | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus"},{"title":"ACL ARR 2025 May | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FMay"},{"title":"Incentives 2026 – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about the ACL Rolling Review scoring system for 2025-2026:\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\nHowever, the search results don't provide the specific 1-5 scale details for the overall assessment score in the review form itself. The results indicate that reviewers use these three scoring dimensions, but the exact numerical scale definitions for the overall recommendation score are not fully detailed in the retrieved content.\n\nIf you need more specific information about the exact scale definitions (what 1-5 means for each score), you may want to visit the official ARR review form directly at aclrollingreview.org/reviewform or check the full reviewer guidelines on aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines."],"durationSeconds":4.524196132999998}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017aAJdkKT6Y32UEfzn7EH1y","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"site:aclrollingreview.org reviewform overall assessment soundness\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Action Editor Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/actioneditorform\"},{\"title\":\"Response to ACL 2023 Questions\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/ACL-2023-session/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Changelog\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/changelog\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Incentives 2026\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026\"},{\"title\":\"Arr Changes December\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/ARR-changes-December/\"}]\n\nI found results for your search query. The search returned information about the ACL Rolling Review (ARR) review form and related guidelines.\n\nThe main result from the ARR review form page (aclrollingreview.org/reviewform) shows that reviewers are asked to assess whether papers are \"sufficiently sound and thorough\" and whether they \"clearly state scientific claims and provide adequate support for them.\"\n\nThe review form includes specific guidance for different paper types: for experimental papers, reviewers consider \"the depth and/or breadth of the research questions investigated, technical soundness of experiments, methodological validity of evaluation,\" while for position papers and surveys they consider \"whether the current state of the field is adequately represented and main counter-arguments acknowledged,\" and for resource papers they consider \"the data collection methodology, resulting data & the difference from existing resources are described in sufficient detail.\"\n\nThe form also includes a soundness rating scale, with ratings ranging from 5 (Excellent: \"This study is one of the most thorough I have seen, given its type\"), 4 (Strong: \"This study provides sufficient support for all of its claims\"), to 3 (Acceptable: \"This study provides sufficient support for its main claims\").\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ef33cb85-ae55-46f6-8462-dd61be87818f","uuid":"97dc38e3-f09e-498f-97a4-d8959d00c0fc","timestamp":"2026-05-15T14:17:15.055Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"site:aclrollingreview.org reviewform overall assessment soundness","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_015t3NHZSNFSqw3xHxhwwtt4","content":[{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"Action Editor Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/actioneditorform"},{"title":"Response to ACL 2023 Questions","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/ACL-2023-session/"},{"title":"ARR Changelog","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/changelog"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"Incentives 2026","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026"},{"title":"Arr Changes December","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/ARR-changes-December/"}]},"I found results for your search query. The search returned information about the ACL Rolling Review (ARR) review form and related guidelines.\n\nThe main result from the ARR review form page (aclrollingreview.org/reviewform) shows that reviewers are asked to assess whether papers are \"sufficiently sound and thorough\" and whether they \"clearly state scientific claims and provide adequate support for them.\"\n\nThe review form includes specific guidance for different paper types: for experimental papers, reviewers consider \"the depth and/or breadth of the research questions investigated, technical soundness of experiments, methodological validity of evaluation,\" while for position papers and surveys they consider \"whether the current state of the field is adequately represented and main counter-arguments acknowledged,\" and for resource papers they consider \"the data collection methodology, resulting data & the difference from existing resources are described in sufficient detail.\"\n\nThe form also includes a soundness rating scale, with ratings ranging from 5 (Excellent: \"This study is one of the most thorough I have seen, given its type\"), 4 (Strong: \"This study provides sufficient support for all of its claims\"), to 3 (Acceptable: \"This study provides sufficient support for its main claims\")."],"durationSeconds":8.475632247999995}}
