{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KXLx2T15rhvpjyxQKsRHio","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL Rolling Review reviewform \"overall assessment\" \"1\" \"2\" \"3\" \"4\" \"5\" soundness excitement\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ACL 2023 Acceptance Recommendations - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/overall-recommendation/\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/reviewform.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewform.md\"},{\"title\":\"Program Chairs’ Report on Peer Review at ACL 2023 Anna Rogers}\",\"url\":\"https://aclanthology.org/2023.acl-long.report.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL’23 Peer Review Policies - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-acl23/\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md\"}]\n\nI found information about the ACL Rolling Review (ARR) review form with details on the scoring scales for soundness, excitement, and overall assessment.\n\n## Summary of the ACL Rolling Review Form Scoring:\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n### Soundness Score:\nThe soundness scale includes: 5 = Excellent (one of the most thorough studies), 4 = Strong (provides sufficient support for all claims), and 3 = Acceptable (provides sufficient support for main claims).\n\n### Excitement Score:\nThe excitement scale includes: 5 = Highly Exciting (would recommend to others and/or attend presentation) and 4 = Exciting (would mention to others and/or make effort to attend presentation). Excitement is subjective and does not necessarily follow what is popular in the field.\n\n### Overall Assessment Score:\nThe overall assessment scale includes: 5 = Consider for Award, 2 = Resubmit next cycle, and 1 = Do not resubmit. The overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper if it were committed to an *ACL venue, reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ef33cb85-ae55-46f6-8462-dd61be87818f","uuid":"ea3f9fe4-54b9-4807-9f6b-c824f6ce2538","timestamp":"2026-05-15T14:17:28.182Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review reviewform \"overall assessment\" \"1\" \"2\" \"3\" \"4\" \"5\" soundness excitement","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_012zBAdkJErH4bBt6Lfs1Drx","content":[{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"ACL 2023 Acceptance Recommendations - ACL 2023","url":"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/overall-recommendation/"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/reviewform.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewform.md"},{"title":"Program Chairs’ Report on Peer Review at ACL 2023 Anna Rogers}","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2023.acl-long.report.pdf"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"ACL’23 Peer Review Policies - ACL 2023","url":"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-acl23/"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md"}]},"I found information about the ACL Rolling Review (ARR) review form with details on the scoring scales for soundness, excitement, and overall assessment.\n\n## Summary of the ACL Rolling Review Form Scoring:\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n### Soundness Score:\nThe soundness scale includes: 5 = Excellent (one of the most thorough studies), 4 = Strong (provides sufficient support for all claims), and 3 = Acceptable (provides sufficient support for main claims).\n\n### Excitement Score:\nThe excitement scale includes: 5 = Highly Exciting (would recommend to others and/or attend presentation) and 4 = Exciting (would mention to others and/or make effort to attend presentation). Excitement is subjective and does not necessarily follow what